<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems-of-conquest">Emblems of Conquest for Retribution Paladin Phase 2</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45624/emblem-of-conquest">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_championsgrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Conquest</span></a> drop from both 10 and 25 man Ulduar.  This can be exchanged for Tier Helm and Chest tokens, as well as neck, waist, ands, legs, and Librams.  <br/>
<br/>Your real priority is just acquiring the tier pieces.  You aren't really going to want to go after the helm long term, however acquiring the tier helm early would still be a pretty large upgrade overall, so after the chest thats probably your best bet.  After that theres a few pieces you can grab to help out the gearing process but you will replace everything on this list minus the chest before 25m Hard modes.  Its important to note that none of these items show up in the absolute bis sets simply due to the power level of 252 ilvl gear.  Your last option is going to be using this on <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45087/runed-orb">
