<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="p2-gear-for-p3">Strong P2 gear for going into P3</h3>A small thing to touch on is noting any gear from Ulduar that will be useful in and throughout P3.  For the retribution paladin, we will not have any items from P2 that are BIS in P3, however we will have a number of items that will come "close" to their P3 counterpart and will be used at least until the heroic (258) versions are acquired:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45663/armbands-of-bedlam">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_23a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Armbands of Bedlam</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46095/soul-devouring-cinch">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_37c.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul-Devouring Cinch</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45599/sabatons-of-lifeless-night">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sabatons of Lifeless Night</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45473/embrace-of-the-gladiator">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Embrace of the Gladiator</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45472/warhelm-of-the-champion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_134.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warhelm of the Champion</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="gemming">Gemming your Gear</h3>When gemming your gear you want to keep in mind a few basic notes:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Jewelcrafting is BIS for you.  This will give you a bonus of 54 to what ever stats you gem, where as blacksmithing will give you only 32.  With this you will want to make sure you are always running 3 <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42225/dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon's Eye</span></a> gems.  These can be purchased with your <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=61/dalaran-jewelcrafters-token">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_variety_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dalaran Jewelcrafter's Token</span></span></a>.  Ideally these should all be <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42142/bold-dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Dragon's Eye</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Never be afraid to gem for hit. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42156/rigid-dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Dragon's Eye</span></a> will provide about 1% hit, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40014/rigid-autumns-glow">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_26.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Autumn's Glow</span></a> provides about .45% hit, and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40038/etched-monarch-topaz">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Etched Monarch Topaz</span></a> will provide ~.24% hit.  These are great ways to make up for a few points missing in a great gear setup otherwise.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Because you want to be running <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41398/relentless-earthsiege-diamond">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_shadowspirit_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relentless Earthsiege Diamond</span></a>, you will only ever need one blue gem, which you should supply by using a single <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49110/nightmare-tear">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_pearl_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nightmare Tear</span></a>.  This gem provides more strength than a <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40022/sovereign-twilight-opal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_29.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sovereign Twilight Opal</span></a> and provides agility on top of it. Use this to fill the highest strength blue socket you have available.  If none is available, look for an attackpower socket next.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Almost all other gems will be <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=39996/bold-scarlet-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Scarlet Ruby</span></a>.  The only time you should deviate from this after hit cap is if you can get a yellow socket with 4 strength per yellow socket bonus.  If thats the case you can fill it with <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40037/inscribed-monarch-topaz">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Monarch Topaz</span></a>.</div></li></ol>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="gearing-in-ulduar">Gearing in Ulduar</h3>With ulduar the main question in play is are are 25man hard modes going to be available to you early on or later. If later you may want to take the advice here and look at the non-252 gear setups and run that route while your guild is gearing up.  Decision descriptions have also been broken up based on what gear is available and what is good.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Retribution Paladin Phase 2</h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="head">Head for Retribution Paladin Phase 2</h3>You are likely going to be stuck going for the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45993/mimirons-flight-goggles">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_newgoggles.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mimiron's Flight Goggles</span></a> for a while, waiting on the DKs to get their <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45472/warhelm-of-the-champion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_134.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warhelm of the Champion</span></a>.  If you're going to be waiting a while to get to mimiron firefighter in 10man, running <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46156/conquerors-aegis-helm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_97.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conqueror's Aegis Helm</span></a> is still not terrible, yielding only 35ish dps lower.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Helm Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50367/arcanum-of-torment">
